er exonerated  at the end of the clone wars vader picks  up one of the blue lightsabers he gifted  to ahsoka amongst the remains of the  crashed star destroyer and lights it up  before walking  away believing that ahsoka is dead of  course  she's still alive and when ahsoka  appears in star wars rebels  she wields different sabers the same  white ones  seen in the mandalorian ahsoka is unique  in the star wars universe because while  she no longer  identifies as a jedi she also hasn't  turned to the dark side  as clone wars executive producer and  mandalorian director dave filoni  previously explained  ahsoka's white lightsabers are meant to  show that she is neither a jedi nor a  sith  revenge is not the jedi way  i am no jedi while there's a clear  element of metaphor at play with  ahsoka's lightsabers  there's also a definitive reason why her  twin weapons are white  in ik johnston's 2016 novel ahsoka  the author fills in the gap between the  clone wars and rebels  prior to reappearing in rebels ahsoka  defeats an inquisitor and takes his  lightsaber crystals  because he is a sith his crystals were  corrupted but ahsoka heals them and  realigns them with force  this turns them white a symbol not only  of their restored purity  but also of ahsoka leaving the order  behind to fight for good in her own way  while the mandalorian marked her first  live-action appearance in the franchise  ahsoka has been hugely influential in  the world of star wars for years  not only is she the first major female  jedi audiences  spent time with on screen she's also a  fan favorite whose decision to turn her  back on the order  but not on fighting against evil makes  her a uniquely complex trailblazer  within the world of the franchise  in an april 2020 interview with vanity  fair dave filoni explained the  significance of ahsoka's choice to  separate from the order  saying she's not a jedi not because she  couldn't be but because she chose a  different path  ahsoka choosing to leave the jedi order  was one of the most powerful moments of  the clone wars series  and i think is one of the most important  stories in all of star wars  she left the order but she didn't stop  helping people she went her own way  and helped take down the empire so i  wouldn't call her a jedi or a padawan  she's a hero check out one of our newest  videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite star wars legends are coming  soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one


